## [ ] T04 · Make ESC stop deleting other windows

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
`keyboard-escape-quit` works through a chain of fallbacks, and its
documented last step is "go back to just one window (by deleting all but the
selected window)". So when nothing else is active (no region, no minibuffer,
no prefix argument, no recursive edit), ESC deletes every other window in
the frame. People press Escape reflexively just to make sure nothing is
pending. That habitual press destroys a deliberately built layout: code next
to a helpful buffer, magit next to a diff, compilation output next to the
source, or the two dired panes that `dired-dwim-target t` is configured for.
`winner-undo` (C-c <left>) can restore it, but only if you notice what
happened and remember the key. The comment in dk-keymap.el says ESC works
"like C-g", which is wrong: C-g never touches windows. The review confirmed
2 windows became 1 after a single ESC.

Why an advice rather than a new command: corfu's popup keymap remaps
`keyboard-escape-quit` to `corfu-reset`, and other packages may remap it
too. A new command bound to <escape> would bypass those remaps, and ESC
would stop closing the completion popup. Advising the existing command keeps
its identity and every remap, and it also covers the built-in ESC ESC ESC
sequence. Temporarily rebinding `one-window-p` to `always` during the call
makes only the "delete other windows" branch unreachable and leaves every
other branch exactly as before. Because the advice is a named function,
adding it again on reload changes nothing, and it can be removed cleanly.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- ESC is safe to press at any time and never changes the window layout.
- ESC still cancels everything it cancels today: region, prefix argument,
  minibuffer, recursive edit, and the corfu popup.
- The comment describes the real behaviour.

TASK (as in fix.prompt)
-----------------------

Files: src/dk-functions.el, src/dk-keymap.el (~10-12)
Problem: `<escape>` runs `keyboard-escape-quit`, which calls
`delete-other-windows` when there is nothing else to cancel (verified: 2
windows -> 1).  The comment claims it works "like C-g".
Change:
  - Keep `<escape>` bound to `keyboard-escape-quit` (so corfu's
    `[remap keyboard-escape-quit]` keeps working) and add a named :around
    advice in dk-functions.el:
      (defun dk/escape-quit-keep-windows (orig-fun &rest args)
        "Run ORIG-FUN (`keyboard-escape-quit') without deleting windows."
        (cl-letf (((symbol-function 'one-window-p) #'always))
          (apply orig-fun args)))
    `(require 'cl-lib)` at the top of dk-functions.el if not present.
  - Install it in dk-keymap.el next to the binding with `advice-add`
    (idempotent on reload).  Fix the comment: ESC now cancels the region,
    prefix argument, minibuffer and recursive edit, but never touches the
    window layout.
Verify (batch): split window, call `keyboard-escape-quit` -> still 2
windows; with an active region, ESC deactivates it.  Manual (GUI): ESC in a
minibuffer aborts it; ESC with a corfu popup closes the popup; ESC ESC ESC
also keeps windows.
Commit: "Keep window layout when ESC quits"
