## [ ] T08 · Stop corfu from hijacking RET  [ASK]

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
With `corfu-auto` the popup appears on its own while you type. With `corfu-
preselect :first` the first candidate is always selected. In corfu's popup
keymap, RET is `corfu-insert`. Together this means that whenever a popup
happens to be visible and you press RET for a newline, corfu inserts the
selected candidate instead and you get no newline. In prose, typing "the"
and RET gives "there". In code, `return x` and RET can become `return xs`.
In a comint or shell buffer, RET inserts a candidate instead of sending the
command. This is the most commonly reported corfu pitfall, and corfu's own
README lists exactly these remedies: unbind RET, preselect the prompt, or
keep RET only in certain modes.

This config already binds TAB to `corfu-insert`, so RET is not needed for
accepting candidates. Option 2 keeps the IDE-style RET in code, where people
are used to it, while protecting prose and shells. The current comment says
RET is corfu's default and "not restated". After the change, the comment
must state the new rule.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- RET is predictable: it always inserts a newline or sends input (or, with
  option 2, accepts only in code).
- Candidates are accepted deliberately with TAB.
- Shell and REPL prompts behave normally while a popup is open.

TASK (as in fix.prompt)
-----------------------

Files: src/dk-completion.el (~195-218)
Problem: `corfu-auto t` + `corfu-preselect :first` + RET = `corfu-insert`
means RET after a word inserts the first candidate instead of a newline
(prose, code, comint prompts).
Question: "What should RET do while a corfu popup is open?"
  1. (Recommended) Always newline/send; accept candidates with TAB only.
  2. Accept the candidate in prog-mode buffers, newline everywhere else.
  3. Keep the current behaviour (skip).
Decision:
Change:
  - Option 1: in corfu's `:config`, `(keymap-unset corfu-map "RET" t)` (and
    "<return>" if it is bound — check with keymap-lookup first).
  - Option 2: bind "RET" in corfu-map to a menu-item whose :filter returns
    `#'corfu-insert` only when `(derived-mode-p 'prog-mode)`, nil otherwise
    (nil falls through to the normal RET).  Use a named filter function in
    dk-functions.el.
  - Rewrite the `:bind` comment (it currently says RET is corfu's default
    and not restated).
Verify: `(keymap-lookup corfu-map "RET")` matches the decision.  Manual: in
an org buffer type "the" + RET -> newline; TAB still inserts the candidate.
Update cheatsheet.md.
Commit: "Keep RET as newline while corfu is open"
Result:


## [ ] T09 · Quieter completion in prose buffers  [ASK]

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
`cape-dabbrev` completes from words already present in your buffers. In
prose almost every word has dabbrev candidates, so with `corfu-auto` a popup
appears after nearly every word of three or more characters. It covers the
text below the cursor, flickers while you type and, before T08, also stole
RET. In code, popups are valuable because identifiers are long and must be
exact. In natural language you type a word faster than you can pick it from
a list.

`dk/prose-display` already exists as the single hook for prose-specific
display tuning in Org and Markdown, so it is the natural place for this. Why
it works: globalized minor modes are turned on after the major-mode hooks
run. `corfu-mode` installs its auto-popup hook only when `corfu-auto` is
non-nil at the moment it is enabled, so a buffer-local nil set in the major-
mode hook prevents the automatic popups. On-demand completion still works:
TAB, thanks to `tab-always-indent 'complete`, and M-TAB after T06. This is
an [ASK] task because some writers like word completion.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- Distraction-free writing in Org and Markdown.
- Completion is still available on demand in prose.
- Code buffers keep automatic completion exactly as today.

TASK (as in fix.prompt)
-----------------------

Files: src/dk-functions.el (`dk/prose-display`, ~234-237)
Problem: in Org/Markdown, `dk/cape-dabbrev` pops corfu up after every
3-letter word while writing prose.
Question: "How should auto-completion behave in Org/Markdown?"
  1. (Recommended) No auto popup in prose; TAB/M-TAB still completes on demand.
  2. Keep auto popup but only after 5 characters in prose.
  3. Keep current behaviour (skip).
Decision:
Change:
  - Option 1: in `dk/prose-display` add `(setq-local corfu-auto nil)`.
    This works because the globalized corfu mode turns `corfu-mode` on after
    the major-mode hooks, and corfu reads `corfu-auto` when enabling.
  - Option 2: `(setq-local corfu-auto-prefix 5)` instead, and make
    `dk/cape-dabbrev` use `(max 3 corfu-auto-prefix)` for its length gate.
  - Update the docstring.
Verify: in a temp org buffer after `(org-mode)`, check `corfu-auto` (or the
prefix) locally and that `corfu--auto-post-command` is / is not on the
buffer-local `post-command-hook` as expected; a prog buffer is unchanged.
Commit: "Disable auto completion popups in prose"
