## [ ] T12 · Make gfm-view-mode a reversible toggle (and keep q from killing)

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
C-c C-v is bound to `gfm-view-mode`, a read-only rendered view. Once you are
in it, no key leads back to editing: C-c C-v is unbound there (confirmed),
and you have to know to run M-x gfm-mode. Worse, `markdown-view-mode-map`
binds `q` to `kill-current-buffer` (confirmed). In Emacs, `q` is the
universal "leave this view" key in read-only and special buffers (help,
view-mode, magit, and others). Pressing `q` to leave the preview kills the
buffer of the file you were editing. Nothing is lost if it was saved, and
Emacs asks first if it was modified, but you lose point, undo history and
the window arrangement.

A toggle on the same key in both directions is the expected pattern in Emacs
(compare C-x C-q for read-only). One detail needs care: markdown-view-mode
makes the buffer read-only, and switching the major mode does not reset
`buffer-read-only`. Leaving the view must therefore restore writability from
the file's permissions. Otherwise you land back in gfm-mode but still unable
to edit.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- The preview is reversible with one key, in both directions.
- `q` leaves the preview instead of closing the file.
- You never end up stuck in a read-only editing buffer.

TASK (as in fix.prompt)
-----------------------

Files: src/dk-functions.el, src/dk-writing.el (~32-38)
Problem: C-c C-v enters `gfm-view-mode`, nothing leads back, and `q` there
runs `kill-current-buffer` on the file's buffer.
Change:
  - Add `dk/markdown-toggle-view` to dk-functions.el: in a
    `markdown-view-mode`-derived buffer switch to `gfm-mode` and restore
    `buffer-read-only` to `(and buffer-file-name (not (file-writable-p
    buffer-file-name)))` (view mode sets it, and a major-mode switch does
    not reset it); otherwise switch to `gfm-view-mode`.
  - Bind it to C-c C-v in `markdown-mode-map` (replacing `gfm-view-mode`)
    and to C-c C-v and q in `markdown-view-mode-map`.  Confirm that
    `gfm-view-mode-map` inherits these (keymap-lookup); if it does not, bind
    them there as well.
Verify: open a temp .md copy in the sandbox: C-c C-v -> gfm-view-mode,
read-only; C-c C-v again -> gfm-mode, writable; `q` in view mode returns to
gfm-mode and the buffer is still live.  Update cheatsheet.md.
Commit: "Toggle markdown view mode in both directions"
