## [ ] T13 · Show markdown markup while editing  [ASK]

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
`markdown-hide-markup` hides **, _, `, # and link brackets, and `markdown-
hide-urls` replaces URLs with a small anchor symbol. Org has org-appear in
this config, which reveals hidden markup while point is inside an element.
markdown-mode has no equivalent. The hidden characters are invisible text:
cursor motion skips over them, deleting at a boundary removes characters you
cannot see, and you cannot read or edit a URL without toggling hiding for
the whole buffer (C-c C-x C-m). Editing Markdown blind easily leaves
unbalanced emphasis or broken links in the file.

After T12 there is a clean split: the editing buffer shows the source, and
the C-c C-v view shows the rendered result (markdown-view-mode hides markup
on its own; the task verifies this). This is an [ASK] task because hidden
markup is a matter of visual taste.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- What you edit is what is in the file, and links can be edited directly.
- Rendered reading is still one key away.
- Markdown follows the same principle as the Org setup: hide only where it
  cannot get in the way of editing.

