## [ ] T14 · Make Go indentation width consistent with gofmt's tabs

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
Go source is indented with tabs, and gofmt enforces that. How wide a tab
LOOKS is controlled by `tab-width` (default 8). `go-ts-mode-indent-offset`
is a different thing: the number of columns per indentation level that Emacs
computes while you type. With offset 4, `indent-tabs-mode` t and `tab-width`
8 (confirmed in the review):
- level 1 is indented with 4 spaces, because a 4-column indent cannot be
  made of 8-wide tabs;
- level 2 gets one tab (8 columns);
- level 3 gets a tab plus 4 spaces.
On save, apheleia runs gofmt, which rewrites leading whitespace to one tab
per level. Level 1 becomes one tab displayed 8 wide. So code that looked 4
wide while you typed jumps to 8 wide after every save, and between saves the
file contains mixed whitespace. The config's comment calls the offset "how
wide one is displayed", a misunderstanding that hides the bug.

Setting `tab-width` to the offset, buffer-locally in Go buffers, makes one
level equal one tab displayed 4 wide, both while typing and after gofmt. The
file content stays canonical gofmt output.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- Stable visual indentation in Go: no jump after saving.
- No mixed tabs and spaces between saves.
- The comment correctly explains the two settings.
- gofmt output is unchanged.

TASK (as in fix.prompt)
-----------------------

Files: src/dk-functions.el, src/dk-languages.el (~126-137)
Problem: `go-ts-mode-indent-offset 4` is the indent step, not the tab
display width (the comment is wrong).  `tab-width` stays 8 with
`indent-tabs-mode t`, so typed lines get 4 spaces, gofmt rewrites them as
tabs shown 8 wide, and indentation jumps after each save.
Change:
  - Add `dk/go-ts-tab-width` (dk-functions.el): `(setq-local tab-width
    go-ts-mode-indent-offset)`.
  - `:hook (go-ts-mode . dk/go-ts-tab-width)` in the go-ts-mode form.
  - Correct the comment: offset = indent step, tab-width set to match so one
    level = one tab displayed 4 wide; gofmt output unaffected.
Verify: in a temp buffer `(go-ts-mode)` (needs the go grammar; otherwise
call the hook function directly in a buffer with indent-tabs-mode t) ->
`tab-width` 4.
Commit: "Display Go tabs at the configured indent width"
Result:


## [ ] T15 · Default to spaces for indentation

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
`indent-tabs-mode` defaults to t. Whenever indentation reaches `tab-width`
(8) columns, Emacs uses a tab character. With 4-column indent steps (C
through `c-ts-mode-indent-offset`, nested Emacs Lisp), deeper lines get
mixtures of tabs and spaces. Diffs then show whitespace changes, code looks
misaligned in tools that render tabs at a different width (web code viewers,
terminals, other editors), and collaborators' linters complain. clang-format
would normalize this only where a .clang-format exists (see T07), so most C
files keep the mixture.

Your current config files contain no tabs (checked), probably because they
were mostly edited outside Emacs. Editing them in Emacs would start
introducing tabs. Modes whose file formats need tabs set `indent-tabs-mode`
back buffer-locally (makefile modes, go-ts-mode), so a global nil is safe;
the task verifies that. Projects with a tab convention can set it in their
own .dir-locals.el.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- Consistent space indentation everywhere except where the file format
  requires tabs.
- Cleaner diffs and the same appearance in every tool.

TASK (as in fix.prompt)
-----------------------

Files: src/dk-defaults.el
Problem: `indent-tabs-mode` is never set (default t), so lines typed in C,
Elisp and other modes mix tabs and spaces at >= 8 columns.
Change: `(setq-default indent-tabs-mode nil)` in dk-defaults.el with a
comment: modes whose formats need tabs (go-ts-mode, makefile modes) set it
back buffer-locally; per-project tab conventions belong in .dir-locals.el.
Verify: default value nil; in temp buffers `(makefile-mode)` -> t,
`(go-ts-mode)` -> t (or confirm in Emacs source that go-ts-mode sets
`indent-tabs-mode` locally), `(c-ts-mode)`/`(emacs-lisp-mode)` -> nil.
Commit: "Indent with spaces by default"
Result:


