M-o is `other-window` globally in this config, a fundamental navigation key
used constantly. `ibuffer-mode-map` binds M-o to `ibuffer-visit-
buffer-1-window` (confirmed). C-x C-b opens ibuffer, usually in another
window, which is exactly where you would press M-o to get back to your code.
Instead, M-o there opens the buffer at point and deletes all other windows,
the same kind of layout damage as T04. Major-mode keymaps shadow the global
map, so the global binding cannot help. Binding M-o in `ibuffer-mode-map`
restores consistency. The shadowed ibuffer command is still available
through M-x and ibuffer's menu.

