## [ ] T18 · Make C-c e (eval-buffer) Elisp-only

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
`eval-buffer` reads the current buffer as Emacs Lisp and evaluates every
form in it. Bound globally to C-c e, it fires in any buffer. A mistyped C-c
e in a Markdown, C, shell or configuration file makes Emacs read that file
as Lisp. Usually it stops with an error at the first symbol, but content
that looks like Lisp (parenthesized expressions in notes, code samples,
Scheme or Common Lisp files) can be partly executed, with side effects,
before the error. The command is only meaningful in Emacs Lisp buffers, so
per AGENTS.md it belongs in `emacs-lisp-mode-map` through a use-package
declaration. The *scratch* check makes sure the key keeps working where it
is used most.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- No accidental evaluation of non-Lisp buffers.
- The key stays available in Emacs Lisp and *scratch* buffers.
- Keybinding placement follows the repository's conventions.

TASK (as in fix.prompt)
-----------------------

Files: src/dk-keymap.el (~47), src/dk-programming.el, cheatsheet.md
Problem: `C-c e` evaluates any buffer as Lisp — Markdown, C, shell files.
Change: remove the global binding; add `(use-package elisp-mode :ensure nil
:bind (:map emacs-lisp-mode-map ("C-c e" . eval-buffer)))` in
dk-programming.el.  Check whether `lisp-interaction-mode-map` inherits from
`emacs-lisp-mode-map` in Emacs 31 (`keymap-parent`); if not, bind it there
too so *scratch* keeps the key.
Verify: `(keymap-lookup (current-global-map) "C-c e")` nil; lookup in
emacs-lisp-mode-map and in a *scratch*-mode buffer -> `eval-buffer`.
Commit: "Bind eval-buffer only in Emacs Lisp buffers"
Result:


## [ ] T19 · Trust the config's own files so Elisp flymake works

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
Emacs 30.1 introduced `trusted-content` as a security fix (CVE-2024-53920).
flymake's Emacs Lisp byte-compile backend expands macros, which executes
code from the file being checked, so merely opening a malicious .el file
with flymake enabled could run code. Since then that backend is disabled in
buffers that are not trusted. This config enables flymake for every prog-
mode buffer, so in Emacs Lisp buffers you would expect live byte-compiler
warnings: free variables, wrong argument counts, obsolete or unknown
functions. That is the most useful feedback when editing your configuration.

But `trusted-content` is nil (confirmed), so `(trusted-content-p)` is nil
for src/*.el (confirmed) and those diagnostics never appear, without any
notice. The stale-advice warning found in the review would have been flagged
in the editor.

The task trusts only files you write and already execute at every startup
(src/, test/, init.el, early-init.el), so trusting them adds no risk. It
deliberately does not trust the whole configuration directory: themes
collected from various sources and package sources under elpa/ are not your
code, and including them would widen trust for no benefit. Appending rather
than assigning keeps any value set through Customize.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- Live byte-compiler diagnostics while editing the configuration.
- The security protection stays in place for every other file.
- Mistakes like the stale advice are caught as you type, not by a review.

TASK (as in fix.prompt)
-----------------------

Files: src/dk-programming.el (flymake section)
Problem: since Emacs 30 `elisp-flymake-byte-compile` only runs in buffers
covered by `trusted-content`; it is unset, so `(trusted-content-p)` is nil
for src/*.el and the config gets no byte-compile diagnostics.
Change: add the config's own sources, abbreviated, to `trusted-content`
(append, do not clobber): "src/", "test/" (directory entries end in "/"),
"init.el", "early-init.el" — each via
`(abbreviate-file-name (expand-file-name X user-emacs-directory))`.  Do NOT
trust the whole user-emacs-directory (elpa, themes from elsewhere).
Comment why.
Verify: in a buffer visiting the real path of src/dk-ui.el (batch, with
`buffer-file-name` set, `emacs-lisp-mode`), `(trusted-content-p)` is t;
for a file in /tmp it is nil.
Commit: "Trust config sources for Elisp flymake"
