## [ ] T30 · Remove stale code and comments

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
Stale code: the `advice-remove` of `dk/eglot-clean-haskell-markdown` was
kept to clean up an old advice in long-running sessions after a reload. That
function no longer exists anywhere, every running session has been restarted
since, and the line produces the only byte-compile warning in the config. A
permanent warning trains you to ignore warnings, while AGENTS.md asks you to
inspect them on every change.

Stale notes:
- Comments written for Emacs 30.2 say "re-add on Emacs 31+". You are on 31.1
  now, so each note is either an open to-do or simply wrong. Checking with
  `boundp` settles which, and reporting the result to you instead of re-
  adding the settings respects the "no new functionality" rule.
