## [ ] T31 · Guard dk/package-list against drift with a test

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
`dk/package-list` exists so `dk/install-packages` can provision everything
up front, on a new machine or in batch. Every third-party use-package has to
be listed there by hand as well, and nothing checks that the two match. Add
a use-package and forget the list, and provisioning misses it (it is
installed lazily at startup instead, which fails offline). Remove a use-
package and forget the list, and an unused package keeps being installed.

They matched at review time, but the next edit can break that silently. An
ERT test that reads src/*.el and compares the two sets turns drift into a
failing test. That follows the AGENTS.md testing guideline: ERT tests under
test/ for testable logic. The parser must recurse because the flyspell
declaration sits inside a `let`. `:ensure nil` marks built-in packages,
which must not be listed.

