## [ ] T32 · Let xref wait for a starting server from sibling buffers (optional)  [ASK]

WHY THIS TASK EXISTS
--------------------
`dk/xref-wait-for-eglot` fixes a startup race. Right after a file is opened,
Eglot is still connecting. M-. would then fall back to the etags backend,
which prompts for a TAGS file or gives wrong results. The wait is keyed on
`dk/eglot-connecting-server`, a buffer-local variable set only in the buffer
that triggered the connection. Other buffers of the same project opened
during startup (a second file opened while the server initializes, or
several buffers restored at once) do not have it, so an early M-. from them
still falls through.

Recording starting servers globally, with their project root and major mode,
lets any buffer of that project wait. Only public APIs are used, so Eglot
updates cannot break it. The task is optional, and skipping is recommended
unless you actually hit the race: it adds complexity to timing-sensitive
code for a benefit limited to the first seconds after a server starts.

WHAT IMPLEMENTING IT ACHIEVES
-----------------------------
- Navigation behaves the same in every buffer of a project while its
  language server starts.

TASK (as in fix.prompt)
-----------------------

Files: src/dk-vars.el, src/dk-functions.el (~187-217), test/dk-functions-test.el
Problem: `dk/eglot-connecting-server` is buffer-local to the buffer that
triggered the connection; other buffers of the same project opened during
startup jump straight to the etags fallback.
Question: "Extend the xref startup wait to all buffers of the project?"
  1. Yes.
  2. No (skip) — recommended if early jumps from other buffers are rare.
Decision:
Change (option 1): record (SERVER ROOT MODE) in a global list
`dk/eglot-starting-servers` from `eglot-server-initialized-hook` (ROOT from
`(project-root (project-current))` in the triggering buffer, MODE its major
mode); prune entries whose server is no longer running or that became
managed; `dk/eglot-connecting-p` also returns non-nil when a live entry has
the current buffer's project root and `(derived-mode-p MODE)`.  Use only
public API (no eglot-- internals).  Extend the tests.
Verify: ERT including a new case for a sibling buffer.
Commit: "Wait for a starting LSP server from any project buffer"
